00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:15.300
Back in the day used to have to basically turn on all these things one by one and dial them in until they looked real

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:16.440
It was all just hacks

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:20.520
So these days if you learn a physically based rendering program like Octane or Redshift

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:23.040
Octane is our renderer. We love Octane

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:26.540
It actually makes it much, much, easier to make something like this look real

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.040
In fact, it takes a lot of the work out.

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:31.200
Octane, just turn it on put it in a light and it's like well that looks awesome.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.380
It feels like cheating at first and then your, just like:

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:34.040
This is it

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:35.120
This is all I needed.

00:14:35.380 --> 00:14:39.880
But this is like where the technology's gotten to, which is wonderful because it's all just there already

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:43.880
just turn it on and simulate it and that's the beautiful thing about it

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:48.340
It just gets technology out of the way for the artist and just lets artists create

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:50.840
and I think Astartes is one of the best examples of that.

